# T7 LauncherKeys: the launcher-started game takes the INI [keys] binding and the [controls] stick dead zone.
# Pre-written build/Route/<run>/appdata/Sunshine/settings.ini: "[launcher] last_image=<disc>", "[controls] stick_deadzone=35",
# "[keys] STICK_UP=23" (T). Made by the capture run t6_cap (99_launcher_capture.dev), so that run is the input here.
# Run (from sunshine-pc): python tools/route.py Strict tools/routes/99_launcher_keys.dev --no-dvd --appdata-from t6_cap --name t6_ls
#   SUNSHINE_DEV_LAUNCHER_ACTIONS=start SUNSHINE_DEV_VPAD=1 SUNSHINE_DEV_START=dolpic/0 SUNSHINE_DEV_SKIP_MOVIES=1 SUNSHINE_DEV_SEED=1
# Evidence: Mario's position in the `log` lines. W (STICK_UP=26 default) must not move him, T (23) must. Then the left stick
# at 40/127 (31.5 %) with stick_deadzone=35 must not move him (`[menu] dev vstick:0:40 set (... stickDeadZone=11468)`).
waitfor director mario dirstate=4 camDemo=0 timeout=3000
wait frames=60
log
menu key:W:down
wait frames=45
menu key:W:up
wait frames=15
log
menu key:T:down
wait frames=45
menu key:T:up
wait frames=45
log
menu vstick:0:40
wait frames=60
log
menu vstick:0:0
wait frames=30
log
end
